{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"source": "data\\documents\\csv\\QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "filename": "QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "filepath": "data\\documents\\csv\\QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "page": 5, "title": "QA-Kaggle-dataset-2024_utf8.csv", "year": "2024", "row": 4}, "page_content": "\ufeffWhat is psoriasis and what are its common symptoms?: What are the common causes of acne?\nPsoriasis is a chronic autoimmune condition that results in the overproduction of skin cells. This overproduction leads to patches of thick, red skin covered with silvery scales. Common symptoms include red patches of skin covered with thick, silvery scales, small scaling spots (commonly seen in children), dry and cracked skin that may bleed, itching, burning, or soreness, thickened, pitted, or ridged nails, and swollen and stiff joints.: Acne is primarily caused by:\r\n\r\n1. Overproduction of oil (sebum) by the skin.\r\n2. Irregular shedding of dead skin cells resulting in irritation of the hair follicles of your skin.\r\n3. Buildup of bacteria.\r\n4. Hormonal changes, particularly during puberty and menstrual cycles.\r\n5. Certain medications, such as corticosteroids, testosterone, or lithium.\r\n6. Diet, especially dairy products and carbohydrate-rich foods.\r\n7. Stress, which can make acne worse.\r\n\r\nIt's important to note that acne is not caused by dirt, and scrubbing the skin too hard or cleansing with harsh soaps or chemicals irritates the skin and can make acne worse.", "type": "Document"}}